Q1. Which command displays the current working directory?
A) pwd

Q2. What permission does 'chmod 755 file.sh' set?
A) rwxr-xr-x

Q3. Write the command to list all files, including hidden ones, in long listing format.
Command: ls -la

Q4. Which symbol represents the current user's home directory?
B) ~

Q5. The command 'chown user:group file' changes what?
B) File owner and group

Q6. Write a command to create a directory named 'project' without an error if it already exists
Command: mkdir -p project

Q7. What does '.' refer to when used as in 'cd .'?
A) Parent directory

Q8. Which command changes ownership of a directory and everything inside it, recursively?
B) chown -R

